                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ethopoeiae"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "63fb7345-2359-4f5a-b225-49c039ea44c6",
                        "entry_id": "b2d6cd38-4e54-3792-817c-118dc19a789a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ethopoeias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "acf5c152-a1af-3b1b-ba5b-79e99a1aa18b",
                        "entry_id": "b2d6cd38-4e54-3792-817c-118dc19a789a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A rhetorical technique in which the speaker or author presents an imaginary speech by a real person, portraying that person's known characteristics and propensities."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95e71367-01c6-45aa-bf72-a3041fb5040f",
                                "sense_id": "acf5c152-a1af-3b1b-ba5b-79e99a1aa18b",
                                "text": "The situation envisioned is the contest for a prize described in Herodotus 8.123 and cast in the form of ethopoeia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a601b38f-22b2-4b33-907d-3539ea47267a",
                                "sense_id": "acf5c152-a1af-3b1b-ba5b-79e99a1aa18b",
                                "text": "In ancient narrative literature, ethopoeia is a frequently used literary tool."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "680f1acd-a971-485c-b405-df190943792b",
                                "sense_id": "acf5c152-a1af-3b1b-ba5b-79e99a1aa18b",
                                "text": "This is a reference to a type of drama-based pedagogy called ethopoeia, which formed a central component of the humanist grammar school curriculum."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2531a8ea-0078-37e4-bacc-a84fac274303",
                        "entry_id": "b2d6cd38-4e54-3792-817c-118dc19a789a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An instance of this technique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b30fa09c-a967-453c-a5b1-832d71196edd",
                                "sense_id": "2531a8ea-0078-37e4-bacc-a84fac274303",
                                "text": "In their ethopoeias of the ideal lover, de la Torre, Ribera, and Luduefia emphasize, as we have seen, eloquence, good physical proportions, youth, elegance, discretion and honesty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b28f54e2-bad4-4d38-8d5d-a507bd7b1adc",
                                "sense_id": "2531a8ea-0078-37e4-bacc-a84fac274303",
                                "text": "The speeches in the De Gelesuintha all can be described as ethopoeiae, that is speeches intended to communicate the emotional condition of their speakers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e3c9de9-ea95-4f9c-86af-8f73c37bf932",
                                "sense_id": "2531a8ea-0078-37e4-bacc-a84fac274303",
                                "text": "An ethopoeia is delimited by some few arguments from past, present, and future time, while exhortation, as an hypothesis dealing with acknowledged particulars, takes its amplification from final headings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "306d5653-144f-498e-8243-1605b870d320",
                                "sense_id": "2531a8ea-0078-37e4-bacc-a84fac274303",
                                "text": "One of the most elaborate extant examples of this genre is a speech by Libanius, an ethopoeia of Medea as she is about to kill her children."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "237f12eb-c634-4e1b-a032-134b6e732c2c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b2d6cd38-4e54-3792-817c-118dc19a789a",
                        "source_sense_description": "rhetorical technique of creating an imaginary speech",
                        "target_lang_word": "éthopée",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "éthopée",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2bd174b-4897-30c7-925c-9c2a78c62a3f",
                                        "entry_id": "07497c8e-398b-3e28-9ab8-4d1cb42eb772",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figure de pensée qui a pour objet la peinture des mœurs et du caractère d’un personnage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rhetoric"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fe0ad67-25c6-46e6-b691-22b9533000db",
                                                "sense_id": "d2bd174b-4897-30c7-925c-9c2a78c62a3f",
                                                "text": "Ces quatre sources sont nᵒ 1 le besoin ; nᵒ 2 le pléonasme ; nᵒ 3 la métathèse ; nᵒ 4 l’énallage. Parmi les figures de pensées, au nombre de dix-huit, il [Phœbammon] en distingue deux nées du besoin : l’aposiopèse et l’épitrochasmos ; six nées du pléonasme : la prodiorthose, l’épidiorthose, la procatalepse, la paralipse, la diotypose, l’épimone ; six nées de la métathèse : la prosopopée, l’éthopée, la figure appelée μιϰτόν, parce qu’elle tient de l’une et de l’autre, l’interrogation appelée έρώτησις, l’interrogation appelée πεύσις, et la prétérition ; quatre nées de l’énallage : l’ironie, la dubitation, l’allusion satirique, l’apostrophe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bd2afd7-8e19-498b-9c6c-21d8576832ec",
                                                "sense_id": "d2bd174b-4897-30c7-925c-9c2a78c62a3f",
                                                "text": "Il [Alexis Ferro] décline la gamme des Mercedes exaltées par Houellebecq et tient l’éthopée, ou l’art de peindre en quelques traits le caractère d’un personnage, pour la figure de style préférée de Weyergans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
